      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. 1700 mg three times daily is 5100 mg/day, which is well above the usual maximum for metformin. Standard labeling caps immediate-release dosing at about 2550 mg/day, and the usual inpatient ceiling is lower. Normal renal and hepatic function don't change that limit, and the dose carries a risk of lactic acidosis. I also don't know of a standard 1700 mg metformin tablet, so this may be a transcription error. For example, 850 mg TID is a common dose.\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose:\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2550 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- **Another dose**, if you intended a different regimen or have a specific reason for a higher dose. Please give the dose and frequency.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order."
